\subsection{Controller realizations and dissipativity certificates}
\label{AppendixA}
Consider the LMIs \eqref{eq:3:4} which imply strict dissipativity with respect to unstructured quadratic supply rate of the closed loop system \eqref{closed_loop} with \eqref{closed_loop_matrices}. 
We will call the matrix $P$ that satisfies these LMIs \emph{the dissipativity certificate}. 
Here we present some properties of dissipativity certificates $P$, which are instrumental 
for the controller reconstruction procedure.  
\begin{lemma}
\label{lemma3}
Suppose the inequalities \eqref{eq:3:4} hold for the closed-loop system with some controller with state space realization matrices $(\bar{A}_c, \bar{B}_c, \bar{C}_c, \bar{D}_c)$, for some unstructured quadratic supply function and with the corresponding dissipativity certificate $\bar{P}$. Let $U \in \mathbb{R}^{n \times n}$ be an arbitrary given regular matrix. Then there exists a regular matrix $L$ such that a controller with the realization 
$(A_c, B_c, C_c, D_c):=(L\bar{A}_c L^{-1}, L \bar{B}_c, \bar{C}_c L^{-1}, \bar{D}_c),$
satisfies \eqref{eq:3:4} with the dissipativity certificate \begin{small}$P:=\begin{pmatrix} X & U \\ U^\top & Q \end{pmatrix}$\end{small}(note that the partition of $P$ is here in conformity with the partition of the closed-loop state vector $\xi$ in \eqref{closed_loop}, that is, $X \in \mathbb{R}^{n \times n}$ and $Q \in \mathbb{R}^{n \times n}$).  
\end{lemma}
\begin{proof} 
Consider the LMIs \eqref{eq:3:4} for the closed-loop system with the controller $(\bar{A}_c, \bar{B}_c, \bar{C}_c, \bar{D}_c)$ and the corresponding dissipativity certificate \begin{small}$\bar{P}:=\begin{pmatrix} X & \bar{U} \\ \bar{U}^\top & \bar{Q} \end{pmatrix}$\end{small}. First we note that we can assume that $\bar{U}$ is a regular matrix. If it is not, due to strict inequalities in \eqref{eq:3:4}, we can always pertube it to a regular matrix. If we use the substitution 
$(\bar{A}_c, \bar{B}_c, \bar{C}_c, \bar{D}_c)=(L^{-1}A_c L, L^{-1} B_c, C_c L, D_c)$
in \eqref{eq:3:4} and then apply the congruence with $\text{diag}(I, L^{-1})$ and $\text{diag}(I,L^{-1}, I )$ respectively on \eqref{E1} and \eqref{E2}, we obtain a new set of LMIs in the form of \eqref{eq:3:4}. These LMIs then certify the strict dissipativity for the controller $(A_c, B_c, C_c, D_c)$ with the dissipativity certificate \begin{small}$P=\begin{pmatrix} X & U \\ U^\top & Q \end{pmatrix}$\end{small} where $U=\bar{U}L^{-1}$, $Q=L^{-\top}\bar{Q} L^{-1}$. It is now clear that by appropriate choice of $L$ we can render arbitrary $U$ from some given $\bar{U}$.      
\end{proof}  
