Since~$N$ is simply-connected, loops representing generators of~$H_1(\Sigma)$ bound immersed discs in~$N$; note that these discs might intersect~$F$, but by general position, and taking the tubular neighbourhood small, we may assume they do not intersect~$\overline{\nu}(\alpha)$.
By performing boundary twists on the immersed discs, we arrange that their framing obstructions vanish; recall Construction~\ref{cons:qF} and Remark~\ref{rem:BoundaryTwist}.
