For this, we recall that the \emph{reduced projective class group}~$\widetilde{K}_0(R)$ of a commutative ring $R$ is the kernel of the rank map~$K_0(R)\to H_0(R)$~\cite[Definition~II.2.3]{WeibelKBook}. 
The inclusion~$H_0(R)\subset K_0(R)$ splits the rank map, so we obtain an isomorphism~$K_0(R)\cong H_0(R)\oplus \widetilde{K}_0(R)$. 
It follows that stably free modules are trivial in $\widetilde{K}_0(R)$ and,  for $R=\Z[G]$ with $G$ finite,  
