Also, $l_{n-2}=zw_0+ xg_1+yg_2$, where $g_1,g_2$ are linear polynomials in $w_j ; 1 \leq j \leq n-1$. Set $ \widetilde{l_{n-2}}=l_{n-2}-zw_0$ where $l_{n-2} \in \mathcal{L}$ is the $(n-2)$-th symmetric equation. 
