By contrast, the Deep BSDE approach, while successful in other high-dimensional applications such as option pricing and hedging, fails to capture the full structure of the optimal policy in our setting—particularly the intertemporal hedging components.



The method’s superior performance—both in scalability and in fidelity to the full structure of the optimal policy—highlights the transformative potential of leveraging PMP through BPTT-derived costate estimates for a broad class of high-dimensional control problems that admit stable costate representations.




