Table~\ref{tab:spectype} provides some statistics on the breakdown of the sample by color and spectral type.  As described above, we have concentrated on K stars, and the 10 year, phase 2 monitoring sample clearly reflects this goal, with K stars comprising nearly 2/3 of the sample.  The size of the monitoring sample was determined by the availability of telescope time, and the desire to observe each star at least once, and preferably a few times, per year for the 10 year duration of the survey.  Particularly for the redder stars, the monitoring sample includes mostly the brighter objects which provide better S/N in our 30 minute exposure times.
