\subsection{\label{sec: response}Monochromatic drive} 
%$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$

In what follows we will consider a monochromatic EMF
\be\label{E}
\mathcal{E}(t)=\mathcal{E}\cos(\omega t)
\ee
of amplitude $\mathcal{E}$ and frequency $\omega$ driving the electron liquid in a Hall-bar of width $2d$, as shown in figure \ref{hall_bar}. As we will show below, in addition to the oscillatory current, the flow of nonreciprocal liquids contains a net DC current which is quadratic in the driving field $\mathcal{E}$. 


